{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-27-Jun-2024-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of students studying in 6 different classes of 6 different schools. The number of students studying in class X from school P forms approximately what percentage of the total number of students studying in class X from all schools together?", "options": [{"text": "32%", "added": false}, {"text": "24%", "added": false}, {"text": "16%", "added": false}, {"text": "8%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "A thief running at 7 km/h is chased by a policeman whose speed is 12 km/h. If the thief is 280 m ahead of the policeman, then the time required for the policeman to catch the thief will be:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The cost price of 36 articles is the same as the selling price of N articles. If the profit is 20%, then the value of N is:", "options": [{"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "articles-and-batches", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "A can do a work in 20 days and B in 30 days. If they work on it together for 2 days, then what is the fraction of the work that is left?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A man wishes to cover 1 km distance in river water. In still water he takes 12 minutes to cover it, but in the flowing river he takes 13 minutes. The speed of the flowing water of the river is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "70%", "added": false}, {"text": "54.64%", "added": false}, {"text": "41.18%", "added": false}, {"text": "60%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A train covers 60 km at a speed of 80 km/h, 100 km at a speed of 90 km/h, and another 140 km at a speed of 120 km/h. Find the average speed for the complete journey. (Round to the nearest integer.)", "options": [{"text": "115 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "99 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "90 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "105 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "100°", "added": false}, {"text": "110°", "added": false}, {"text": "80°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "The base of a parallelogram is twice its height. If the area of the parallelogram is 338 cm2, then find its height (in cm).", "options": [{"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "triangle-and-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "57% of Ranita’s weekly income is equal to 76% of Bhaskar’s weekly income. If Ranita’s weekly income was reduced by ₹400, while Bhaskar’s weekly income did not change, the ratio of the weekly incomes of Ranita and Bhaskar, respectively, would have been 6 : 5. What is Bhaskar’s weekly income (in ₹)?", "options": [{"text": "3000", "added": false}, {"text": "4000", "added": false}, {"text": "2800", "added": false}, {"text": "3200", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "A person borrowed ₹ 1760 at 6% per annum and ₹ 2240 at 9% per annum at simple interest for the same period. He had to pay ₹ 1536 in all as interest. Find the time (in years).", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "quadratic-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Find the value of 12 + 24 ÷ 2 - 7 × 30 ÷ 6 + (5 + 4) × 8 + 8 ÷ 8 - 8.", "options": [{"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "85", "added": false}, {"text": "58", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "46", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Simplify the given expression.", "options": [{"text": "108", "added": false}, {"text": "138", "added": false}, {"text": "126", "added": false}, {"text": "112", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "Ramanna purchased raw materials for a certain price to manufacture a product. However, owing to shortage of labour, 22.5% of the raw materials could not be utilised and got wasted. 80% of the cost of raw materials used was added as the cost of manufacturing. If Ramanna could sell his product at a price to earn an overall profit of 20% after offering a discount of 20%, how many times of the total cost of the raw materials purchased was the marked price of the product?", "options": [{"text": "2.43 times", "added": false}, {"text": "2.40 times", "added": false}, {"text": "2.44 times", "added": false}, {"text": "2.42 times", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Simplify the following expression.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "A shopkeeper offers 3 schemes of discounts to his customers. Which of the following schemes will fetch the minimum discount percentage? A)Two successive discounts of 24% and 27%. B) Buy 5 get three free. C) Buy 6 and get 10.", "options": [{"text": "B", "added": false}, {"text": "A", "added": false}, {"text": "C", "added": false}, {"text": "Both A and C", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "If the radius of a sphere is 2.1 cm, then the volume of sphere is equal to:", "options": [{"text": "38.088 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "36.808 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "38.808 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "36.088 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "225", "added": false}, {"text": "320", "added": false}, {"text": "200", "added": false}, {"text": "195", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "If cotθ =28/45, then find the value of ( sinθ - cosθ ).", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Find the single discount rate percentage equivalent to the successive discounts of 10%, 20% and 20%.", "options": [{"text": "40%", "added": false}, {"text": "42.4%", "added": false}, {"text": "50%", "added": false}, {"text": "54.6%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "A can complete a piece of work alone in 200 days, while B can complete the same piece of work alone in 100 days. In every three-day cycle, both A and B work on day 1, only A works on day 2, and only B works on day 3. This cycle continues till the work is completed. How many days in all does it take the duo to complete the work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "A 12 litre solution of acid and water contains 30% acid. How much water (in litres) must be added to get a solution having 20% acid?", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "70%", "added": false}, {"text": "75%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "If the sum of two numbers x and y is 12 and their product is 27, then find the sum of their cubes.", "options": [{"text": "576", "added": false}, {"text": "657", "added": false}, {"text": "756", "added": false}, {"text": "765", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "The following table shows the classification of 100 students based on the marks obtained by them in Maths and Science in an examination. What is the difference between the number of students who passed with 60 as cut-off marks in Science and those who passed with 60 as cut-off marks in aggregate?", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "478", "added": false}, {"text": "462", "added": false}, {"text": "456", "added": false}, {"text": "470", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "Find the value of 24 ÷ (3 – 8 × 3 + 27) + 3.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "A sum of money at compound interest doubles itself in 4 years. In how many years does the sum become 8 times of itself at the same rate of interest?", "options": [{"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "In an election, 12% of the voters in the voter list did not cast their votes, whereas 84 voters cast their ballot papers blank. There were only two candidates: Ramagya and Shravan. The winner, Ramagya, was supported by 54% of all the voters in the list. He got 1456 more votes than his rival, Shravan. Find the total number of voters in the list.", "options": [{"text": "5690", "added": false}, {"text": "6860", "added": false}, {"text": "6670", "added": false}, {"text": "7860", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "68", "added": false}, {"text": "64", "added": false}, {"text": "74", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "40000", "added": false}, {"text": "50000", "added": false}, {"text": "20000", "added": false}, {"text": "30000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "If sec 6A = cosec (A – 29°), where 2A is an acute angle, then the measure of ∠A = ___°.", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "19", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "In ∆ABC, P is a point on AB such that PB : AP = 3 : 4 and PQ is parallel to AC. If AR and QS are perpendicular to PC and QS = 9 cm, what is the length (in cm) of AR?", "options": [{"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "14", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "The fourth proportional to 4,a and 16a is 81. What is the value of a?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "In an election between two candidates, one got 60% of the total valid votes. 25% of the votes were invalid. If the total number of votes was 15,000, then find the number of valid votes that the other candidate got.", "options": [{"text": "5,000", "added": false}, {"text": "4,500", "added": false}, {"text": "5,550", "added": false}, {"text": "6,750", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "In ∆ABC, AD is the internal bisector of ∠A, meeting the side BC at D. If BD = 5 cm, BC = 7.5 cm, then AB : AC is:", "options": [{"text": "2 : 1", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "1 : 2", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "Two numbers are in the ratio of 3 : 7. If 11 is subtracted from each, the ratio between the numbers becomes 7 : 20. Find the smaller number.", "options": [{"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "A car covers 20 km in the first quarter of an hour, 25 km in the second quarter of that hour and 15 km in the third quarter. The average speed of the car (in km/h) over the entire journey is:", "options": [{"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}, {"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}]}